WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.133
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.501
Thank you so much
for coming back.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.133
-Are you kidding?
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:08.467
-You were here before.
-I was. I was sweating.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.167
-You were sweating --
You were Donna Summer.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.300
-I was.
I was disco Donna Summer,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.234
and I kid you not,
thank you to that one person.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:17.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Only to you.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.734
-It only takes one.
It only takes one.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.901
-No, I remember them saying,

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.234
"Yeah, you're gonna be
on 'Jimmy Fallon,'"

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.434
and I said, "Are you sure
you don't want to do

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:30.300
one of LaChanze's songs,
because she's very famous

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.501
and a really good singer.
-No, you were --

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:35.300
Here you are here. There's a
picture of all of you guys.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.100
All three Donnas.
Yeah.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.501
-Oh, my gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:42.534
Yes! Storm Lever, LaChanze.
But we did "MacArthur Park."

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.334
Yo, yo, yo,
with that fire band over there.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:47.067
-That's right, yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.367
-"MacArthur park."
I mean, loved it.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.801
-Yeah.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:52.901
-And then I found out that
I've seen you even before that.

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.200
-Uh-huh.
-You were in "Hamilton."

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.067
-I was.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.000
I was, I was, I was.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.901
-You were the bullet.
-Yes.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.367
-Now talk to me about this.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:07.067
-Okay, well -- [ chuckles ] --
it's hard.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.400
-Yeah.
-'Cause, spoiler alert, he dies.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.834
-Yes, okay, yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.167
-So when we were rehearsing,
Andy Blankenbuehler was like,

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.567
"Come here, Ari.
You're gonna trace this bullet,

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.067
and the first time,
you're gonna miss him."

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.734
And I said,
"That's awesome, cool.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.734
So I'm gonna just do that?
Great."

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:22.167
He said, "You're gonna do it
a second time,

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:25.367
and then that time,
he's gonna die."

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:29.100
And I was like, "Okay.
I'm playing an inanimate object.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.501
Awesome."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.968
So, as an actor I was like,

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.901
"How do I make this work
for myself," you know?

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:36.834
So I just started
filling in the blanks.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.901
And I said,
"What about an omen of death?"

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:42.667
Maybe she's like, you know,
death itself.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:45.567
-Wow! So you really
made it a character.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.567
-I sure did. And guess what --
no one but me knew that.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.334
In fact, to this day,
I'm pretty sure

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:56.133
the creative team is like,
"What are you talking about?"

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.767
-Yeah, they're like, "Oh,
that's what you were thinking?"

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.434
-Yeah, "How creative of you."

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.367
-But then we get --
Now you're a movie star.

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:07.234
I saw you in "The Prom."
-Yeah.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:08.901
-With Nicole Kidman...
-Uh-huh.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.601
-...Meryl Streep.
-Yeah!

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:13.400
-That's big leagues.
-Yeah, I was stressed

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.968
on that movie too.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.801
No, it was great.
So one of my first days on set

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.100
was actually during
one of Meryl's big numbers,

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.501
called "It's Not About Me."

00:02:24.501 --> 00:02:28.100
And when Meryl is performing,
like, you clap after every take,

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.367
so naturally, I was
very attentive, right?

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.801
And she's killing it, mind you.
-Yeah.

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.868
-So the one time I was like,

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.767
"Oh, I got something
on my skirt. Oh, no.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.100
Let me just clean that off
real quick."

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:45.367
I look up, and she says,
"You're not clapping.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:48.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.334
"Was it not...good."
-"Was it bad?"

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:53.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.567
-Wow! Busted.
-I went full, like, Andy --

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:58.767
"No, no, no, no!
You were great, you were great."

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:01.067
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:02.267
-Yeah!
Of course. Meryl Streep.

00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:05.100
-I literally got on the floor
and bowed

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:08.501
because I was so stressed out!
-Yes!

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.934
"Like, no way I didn't clap.
But, yeah, you're Meryl Streep."

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.167
Come on.
-And you do --

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:15.067
you bow to the queen,
and it all works great.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.601
But she was great.
Everyone was great.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.434
Nicole came and offered me
carrots one day,

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.234
and I will remember that
till the day that I die.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:22.767
-Isn't it weird,
the moments you remember?

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:24.067
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.567
-'Cause you wonder if they
remember those moments.

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:28.033
-Oh, she has no idea.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:32.734
None.
"Ariana, you want a carrot?"

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:36.033
"What?"
"Ariana, you want a carrot?"

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.434
And I was -- "Yeah! I do!"

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.667
-"Yeah, I do!"
-"I do!"

00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:41.434
-"I absolutely
want that carrot!"

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:45.734
-"You give me that carrot!"
-"Carrot right now!"

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.133
You're hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.968
this weekend.
-Yes, I am.

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:50.367
-I know.
Are you now going like,

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.367
"What did I get myself into?"
-Actually, no,

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.033
but I have to tell you,
most of Twitter was like,

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.934
"Cool, cool, cool.
Didn't you just, like,

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:59.033
misspell 'Grande'?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.501
And I was like --
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.801
A-yo!
Here all week.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.767
Actually, just Saturday.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.434
-"I'm here all week.
Or, no, only on Saturday."

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:11.133
-I kid you not, though, there
was one lady, Carol --

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:15.234
poor Carol --
she said, "Who are you?

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:18.934
I don't know who you are.
Explain yourself."

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.300
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.234
-And I was like,
"Oh, this is terrible.

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.868
Well, here's my résumé."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:28.367
-I mean --
You're very acclaimed.

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:29.634
I will tell Carol
exactly who you are.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:32.901
-Dear Carol, I hope you tune in,
and I'm sorry

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.067
you didn't know who I was,

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.501
but I promise
we'll give you a good show.

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.367
-We'll give you a great show,
and you're gonna love

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:39.067
Ariana DeBose.
I want to talk to you about

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:40.534
"West Side Story"
when we come back.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:42.300
More with Ariana.
Come on back, everybody.

